{
  "about": "The emblems: one line glyph for each thing a player chooses or meets by kind (a reason for coming, a life, a people, a calling, a school, a god, a way, what a spell is for), drawn in light, single strokes on a 48 by 48 ground, no letters. Each is keyed by the id of what it stands for, the same in creation, in play and in the Encyclopedia of Imbar; a thing with no emblem here shows its name alone. Each set's `text` gives each emblem as one character (unicode, or an emoji where unicode has no fitting sign), for a client drawn in text (the terminal) or a page with no room for a line glyph: the same thing, said the same everywhere.",
