    "acts": {
      "about": "What the company does of itself, wherever it is: waiting and searching, shown by their glyphs where words would crowd the scene (the owner, 6 November). Waiting is an hourglass: two bulbs meeting at a narrow neck between its caps, sand settled in the upper and heaped in the lower, its two sides never crossing (the owner, 7 November: the first, its sides drawn across each other, read as a twisted ribbon). The rail of the scene (amendment 6): going is a way that bends on into the distance; looking an open eye; the map a sheet folded in four; the book a book lying open.",
